  m_text: "Everything in a scene is a GameObject. A GameObject on its own does nothing: its components do the work. Every GameObject has a Transform, which stores its position, rotation and scale. The Transform cannot be removed.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You create an empty GameObject. Which components will it have?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Choose GameObject \u203A Create Empty.\n2. Select it and read its components in the Inspector.\n3. Right-click the Transform's title bar and look for Remove Component.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual, Introduction to GameObjects; Transforms</color></size>"
