  m_text: 'A GameObject can be the child of another. The child moves, rotates and scales with its parent. A child''s Transform shows its position relative to the parent (local), not to the world origin (world).


    <b>Predict:</b> You move the parent Cart 3 m to the side. What happens to the Position values of its child Box?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Move Cart and watch Box follow it.

    2. Drag Box out of Cart in the Hierarchy and read its Position again.

    3. Drag it back onto Cart.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual, Manage GameObjects in the Hierarchy window</color></size>'
