      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A component gives a GameObject its job. Add a Light component to an empty GameObject and it lights the scene around it. The light has a position and a direction, but no mesh: in the Game view only its effect is visible.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> The empty GameObject Lamp hangs above the bench. You add a Light component to it. What changes?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Lamp, then Add Component \u203A Rendering \u203A Light.\n2. Set Type to Spot and rotate Lamp to point down.\n3. Untick the Light component, then tick it again.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Lights topic, scene Lights, Row 1 \xB7 The light</color></size>"
