  m_text: "Rendering Layers are a second set of groups, used only for drawing. A Mesh Renderer can belong to several. A light lights only the renderers that share one of its Rendering Layers; a Decal Projector reads them the same way. Their names are in Tags and Layers.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> The spot light's Rendering Layers are set to Light Layer 1 only. The left cube is in Default, the right cube in Light Layer 1. Which cube does the spot light reach?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select the left cube and add Light Layer 1 to its Mesh Renderer's Rendering Layer Mask.\n2. Select the spot light and set its Rendering Layers to Everything.\n3. Set it back to Light Layer 1.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 8 \xB7 The four labels compared (this scene)</color></size>"
