  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Every GameObject has one Tag and one Layer, set at the top of the Inspector. A Tag is a name that scripts look for. A Layer is a group the engine reads: a camera's Culling Mask, for example, draws only the Layers it includes.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You put the red cube on a new Layer and untick that Layer in this station camera's Culling Mask. What will the camera show?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. In the red cube's Layer menu, choose Add Layer and add a Layer named Hidden.\n2. Put the red cube on Hidden.\n3. Select Camera - 6 \xB7 Tag and Layer, untick Hidden in its Culling Mask and look at its preview in the Scene view.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 8 \xB7 The four labels compared (this scene)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
