  m_text: 'A visible object needs two components. The Mesh Filter holds the mesh: the shape. The Mesh Renderer draws that mesh with its materials. The Cube in the GameObject menu has both, plus a Box Collider for physics.


    <b>Predict:</b> You switch off this cube''s Mesh Renderer. What is left of the cube in the scene?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Select the cube and untick its Mesh Renderer.

    2. Keep it selected and look at the Scene view.

    3. Tick it again, then set the Mesh Filter''s Mesh to Cylinder.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual, Mesh Filter component reference; Mesh Renderer component reference</color></size>'
